# Daemon-Core architecture

This document defines the canonical architecture of the project.

## Scope

Daemon-Core is a modular desktop shell framework for Linux. It provides the shell layer between the OS and the interactive user experience.

## Stack

- Wayland
- Hyprland
- greetd
- Quickshell
- Qt 6
- QML
- JSON configuration

## Core principles

### Separation of concerns

Each layer has one responsibility.

### Single source of truth

Configuration, theme data, and runtime state must each have exactly one authoritative owner.

### Theme first

Theme values are provided through tokens, not hardcoded in UI components.

### Service-driven architecture

Business logic belongs in services. Components render and respond to state.

### Default-safe behavior

The system must handle invalid or missing state without crashing.

## Layer model

```text
User interface
    ↓
Feature modules
    ↓
Shared components
    ↓
Services
    ↓
IPC adapters
    ↓
System integration
    ↓
Linux / Wayland
```

