## Dependency direction

Dependencies must only move downward.

```text
UI -> Features -> Shared -> Services -> IPC -> System
```

The reverse direction is forbidden.

## Required responsibility split

### Services

- configuration management
- profile management
- theme management
- state management
- notification logic
- power and session logic
- system integration wrappers

### Shared components

- buttons
- cards
- dialogs
- forms
- small reusable UI primitives

### Feature modules

- greeter
- lockscreen
- bar
- dashboard
- notifications
- control center
- wallpaper

### IPC adapters

- Hyprland IPC
- DBus IPC
- PipeWire IPC
- NetworkManager IPC
- BlueZ IPC

## Configuration architecture

Configuration files are centralized under:

```text
~/.config/daemon-core/
```

Canonical files:

```text
config.json
settings.json
state.json
profile.json
theme.json
```

## Configuration resolution order

```text
runtime state
    ↓
user settings
    ↓
profile settings
    ↓
default settings
    ↓
safe fallback
```

## Theme architecture

Each theme lives under:

```text
themes/<theme-id>/
```

Example:

```text
themes/
├── daemon-dark/
├── daemon-light/
└── nord/
```

The active theme must be resolved through `ThemeService`.

## Service contract

Every service must provide:

- properties
- signals
- methods
- validation
- error logging
- graceful fallback behavior

## Safe mode

Safe mode must always remain operational. It must use:

- default theme
- default profile
- minimal enabled services
- enhanced logging

## Security principles

- never store secrets in theme or UI files
- never bypass PAM or greetd for login
- validate external data
- use least privilege

## Implementation note

This repository currently defines the architecture and specification layer before full runtime implementation. The project is intentionally structured to keep the foundation consistent before adding feature-heavy code.



